    <briefdescription>
<para>C++20 concept satisfied when <computeroutput>T</computeroutput> is a framework floating-point wrapper with a tolerance. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>T</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The type to be checked.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
The <computeroutput>has_epsilon</computeroutput> concept is satisfied when <computeroutput>T</computeroutput> is a framework expression type (see <computeroutput>is_op</computeroutput>) with an <computeroutput>epsilon</computeroutput> member, like <computeroutput><ref refid="structmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1type__traits_1_1floating__point__constant" kindref="compound">floating_point_constant</ref></computeroutput> and the floating-point specialisation of <computeroutput><ref refid="structmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1type__traits_1_1value" kindref="compound">value</ref>&lt;T&gt;</computeroutput>. The comparators treat the operands within this tolerance as equal; a custom comparator uses it to do the same.</para>
<para>The types of the application are excluded, even if they have a member named <computeroutput>epsilon</computeroutput>, so that they are compared with their own operators. </para>
